@lang en
IMPORT `cstd-ch2-benefits`

-- Tests for Chapters 3 and 4 (Articles 20 to 32). Every expected value was worked out by hand
-- from the clause cited before it was run. Money in dong.

§ `Tests — Chapters 3 and 4`

§§ `Articles 20 and 21`

-- 20.2: a premium due on 1 March 2026 has a grace period to 30 April 2026 (fork F-20).
#ASSERT `20.2 — the last day of the grace period for a premium due on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#TRACE `20.1 — the duty to pay the premium due` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `pay the premium due` AT 60
#TRACE `20.1 — the duty to pay the premium due` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 61)

-- 21: premium 10 million a period, 1 million a month.
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF TRUE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 0, 0, 0) EQUALS `the premium was paid`
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, TRUE, 10000000, 1000000, 0, 0, 0) EQUALS `Article 21 does not apply: the policyholder asked to terminate`
-- 12 million held covers it.
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 12000000, 0, 0) EQUALS `the premium is paid from the coupons, dividends and interest held`
-- 2 held; cash value 50 less Debt 10 is 40, enough for the 8 short: 8 advanced.
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 2000000, 50000000, 10000000) EQUALS `the shortfall is advanced from the cash value as an automatic premium loan` 8000000
-- Cash value 8, less than a period's 10, but enough for a month: the frequency shortens.
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 0, 8000000, 0) EQUALS `the premium frequency is shortened, at most to monthly, and the premium advanced`
-- Cash value 5 less Debt 4.5 is 0.5, less than a month's 1: the contract lapses.
#ASSERT `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 0, 5000000, 4500000) EQUALS `the contract lapses at the end of the grace period`
-- Cash value 12 covers a period's 10, so no shortening; less Debt 10 it is 2, enough for a
-- month but not for the 10 short: 21.1 cannot advance it, 21.2 neither shortens nor lapses
-- (finding X-15).
#ASSERT REFUSED `21 — the outcome of` (`The position at the end of a grace period` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10000000, 1000000, 0, 12000000, 10000000) BECAUSE "Article 21 does not say what follows when the cash value covers a period's premium but, less the Debt, does not cover the shortfall"

§§ `Articles 22 to 28`

#ASSERT `22 — the payment of` 100000000 `after` 5000000 `,` 10000000 `and` 30000000 EQUALS 55000000
#ASSERT `22 — the payment of` 10000000 `after` 5000000 `,` 10000000 `and` 30000000 EQUALS 0

-- 23: a lapse on 1 January 2026; two years run to 1 January 2028.
#ASSERT `23 — under` `C1` `a request on` (YMD 2028 1 1) `after a lapse on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `is in time`
#ASSERT NOT (`23 — under` `C1` `a request on` (YMD 2028 1 2) `after a lapse on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `is in time`)
-- An insured of 94 Tuổi at the effective date (born 1 July 1925): the term ends at 99 Tuổi, the
-- 5th anniversary, 1 January 2025; a request after it is out of time though within two years.
`C-94` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2020 1 1) `for an insured born` (YMD 1925 7 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT `the maturity date of` `C-94` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT `23 — under` `C-94` `a request on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `after a lapse on` (YMD 2024 6 1) `is in time`
#ASSERT NOT (`23 — under` `C-94` `a request on` (YMD 2025 1 2) `after a lapse on` (YMD 2024 6 1) `is in time`)
#ASSERT `23 — under` `C1` `after a lapse on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `the request of` (YMD 2027 1 1) `meets Article 23:` (`A request for reinstatement` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`23 — under` `C1` `after a lapse on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `the request of` (YMD 2027 1 1) `meets Article 23:` (`A request for reinstatement` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE))
#TRACE `23 — under` `C1` `the right to request reinstatement after a lapse on` (YMD 2026 1 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `request reinstatement in writing` AT 700

#ASSERT `24 — the contract has a cash value: first premium of year 2 paid` TRUE `, premiums paid when due` TRUE `, in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`24 — the contract has a cash value: first premium of year 2 paid` FALSE `, premiums paid when due` TRUE `, in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT `25 — the payment on early termination, of a surrender value of` 30000000 EQUALS 30000000
#ASSERT `25 — the payment on early termination, of a surrender value of` (0 MINUS 5000000) EQUALS 0

-- 26.1: 80% of 100 million is 80 million: 80 allowed, one dong more not; under the minimum not.
#ASSERT `26.1 — a loan bringing the total to` 80000000 `is allowed on a cash value of` 100000000 `, the minimum being` 1000000
#ASSERT NOT (`26.1 — a loan bringing the total to` 80000001 `is allowed on a cash value of` 100000000 `, the minimum being` 1000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`26.1 — a loan bringing the total to` 4000000 `is allowed on a cash value of` 100000000 `, the minimum being` 5000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`26.1 — a loan bringing the total to` 0 `is allowed on a cash value of` 0 `, the minimum being` 0)
-- 26.5: a Debt equal to the cash value does not exceed it; one dong more does.
#ASSERT NOT (`26.5 — the contract lapses: debt with interest` 100000000 `against a cash value of` 100000000)
#ASSERT `26.5 — the contract lapses: debt with interest` 100000001 `against a cash value of` 100000000

#ASSERT REFUSED `27 — the reduced sum insured bought by` 50000000 BECAUSE "Article 27 does not state how the reduced sum insured is computed"
#ASSERT `27 — conversion to a reduced paid-up contract is open, on a cash value of` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`27 — conversion to a reduced paid-up contract is open, on a cash value of` 0)

-- 28.2: effective 1 January 2020: a request on 30 June 2020 is within the first six months;
-- on 1 July 2020 it is not (fork F-28).
#ASSERT `28.2 — under` `C1` `a request on` (YMD 2020 6 30) `to add a rider, offered` TRUE `, the person qualifying` TRUE `, premiums paid` TRUE `, may be granted`
#ASSERT NOT (`28.2 — under` `C1` `a request on` (YMD 2020 7 1) `to add a rider, offered` TRUE `, the person qualifying` TRUE `, premiums paid` TRUE `, may be granted`)
#ASSERT NOT (`28.2 — under` `C1` `a request on` (YMD 2020 6 30) `to add a rider, offered` FALSE `, the person qualifying` TRUE `, premiums paid` TRUE `, may be granted`)

§§ `Article 29`

-- 29.1: an event on 15 March 2026: the claim is in time on 15 March 2027 (fork F-29a), not on
-- the 16th; ten days of force majeure move the last day to 25 March 2027.
#ASSERT `29.1 — the last day to claim for an insured event on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, with days of obstacle` 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 15
#ASSERT `29.1 — a claim for an event on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, with days of obstacle` 0 `, submitted on` (YMD 2027 3 15) `is in time`
#ASSERT NOT (`29.1 — a claim for an event on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, with days of obstacle` 0 `, submitted on` (YMD 2027 3 16) `is in time`)
#ASSERT `29.1 — the last day to claim for an insured event on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, with days of obstacle` 10 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 25
#TRACE `29.1 — the duty to notify the insured event` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `notify the Company of the insured event` AT 3

#ASSERT `29.2 — the death claim documents are complete:` (`The documents for a death claim` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`29.2 — the death claim documents are complete:` (`The documents for a death claim` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE))
#ASSERT `29.3 — the critical illness claim documents are complete:` (`The documents for a critical illness claim` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`29.3 — the critical illness claim documents are complete:` (`The documents for a critical illness claim` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE))

-- 29.4: documents complete on 1 May 2026: pay by 31 May; paid on 5 June, 5 days late; on 31
-- May, none.
#ASSERT `29.4 — the last day to pay a claim whose documents were complete on` (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT `29.4 — the days of delay, documents complete on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and paid on` (YMD 2026 6 5) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `29.4 — the days of delay, documents complete on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `and paid on` (YMD 2026 5 31) EQUALS 0
-- Paid on day 30: discharged. Not by day 31: the duty to pay with interest stands.
-- A refusal not answered in writing by day 31: breach.
#TRACE `29.4 — the Company's duty on a complete claim, approved:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `pay the benefit` AT 30
#TRACE `29.4 — the Company's duty on a complete claim, approved:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
#TRACE `29.4 — the Company's duty on a complete claim, approved:` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

§§ `Articles 30 to 32`

#ASSERT `30.2 — the forums open to a dispute not settled by negotiation` EQUALS LIST `the competent court where the policyholder lawfully resides`, `the competent court where the Company has its head office`
#ASSERT `30.3 — the last day to sue on a dispute arising on` (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2029 5 1

-- 31, on C1 (75 Tuổi at 1 January 2061).
#ASSERT `31 — under` `C1` `the grounds on which the benefit has ended by` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, in force` TRUE `, the late stage approved on` NOTHING EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `31 — under` `C1` `the grounds on which the benefit has ended by` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, in force` FALSE `, the late stage approved on` NOTHING EQUALS LIST `31.1 the contract has lapsed, terminated, been cancelled or matured`
#ASSERT `31 — under` `C1` `the grounds on which the benefit has ended by` (YMD 2061 1 1) `, in force` TRUE `, the late stage approved on` NOTHING EQUALS LIST `31.2 the anniversary at which the insured reaches 75 Tuổi has come`
#ASSERT `31 — under` `C1` `the grounds on which the benefit has ended by` (YMD 2031 1 1) `, in force` TRUE `, the late stage approved on` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) EQUALS LIST `31.3 the Company has approved the late-stage benefit`

-- 32, on C1 (maturity at 99 Tuổi: 34 + 65, 1 January 2085).
GIVEN death   IS A MAYBE DATE
      lapse   IS A MAYBE DATE
      reins   IS A MAYBE DATE
      request IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The facts Article 32 turns on`
`Article 32 facts: death` death `, lapse` lapse `, reinstated` reins `, termination requested` request MEANS
    `The facts Article 32 turns on` OF death, lapse, reins, request, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) `, lapse` NOTHING `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS LIST `32.1 the insured died`
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) `, lapse` NOTHING `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2029 12 31) EQUALS EMPTY
-- 32.2: a lapse on 1 January 2026, not reinstated: still running on 1 January 2028, ended on
-- the 2nd; reinstated on 31 December 2027, not ended.
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` NOTHING `, lapse` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` NOTHING `, lapse` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2028 1 2) EQUALS LIST `32.2 a lapse was not reinstated within 2 years`
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` NOTHING `, lapse` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) `, reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2027 12 31)) `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2028 1 2) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` NOTHING `, lapse` NOTHING `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` (JUST (YMD 2027 5 1))) `, by` (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS LIST `32.3 the policyholder asked for early termination`
#ASSERT `the maturity date of` `C1` EQUALS YMD 2085 1 1
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`Article 32 facts: death` NOTHING `, lapse` NOTHING `, reinstated` NOTHING `, termination requested` NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2085 1 1) EQUALS LIST `32.5 the maturity date`
